2026-11-06T02:56:31.1060990Z [34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
2026-11-06T02:56:31.1069866Z [0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
2026-11-06T02:56:31.1070575Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
2026-11-06T02:56:31.1074492Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
2026-11-06T02:56:31.1074772Z 
2026-11-06T02:56:31.1075382Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
2026-11-06T02:56:31.1075810Z 
2026-11-06T02:56:31.1076105Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
2026-11-06T02:56:31.1076578Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
2026-11-06T02:56:31.1076836Z 
2026-11-06T02:56:31.1077025Z If you would like to
2026-11-06T02:56:31.1077388Z see the output, try like this:
2026-11-06T02:56:31.1077595Z 
2026-11-06T02:56:31.1077863Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
2026-11-06T02:56:31.1078381Z   $ sh ./install-nix
2026-11-06T02:56:31.1078543Z 
